WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:02.310
Hey, Thoughty2 here.

00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:08.009
The placebo effect is one of the least understood
phenomenon known to man.

00:00:08.009 --> 00:00:14.669
In some cases this purely psychological effect
has the power to completely heal people.

00:00:14.669 --> 00:00:22.960
But how does it work?

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:27.360
The word Placebo comes from the latin "I will
please".

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:34.359
There have been endless studies proving that
the placebo effect works, in some clinical

00:00:34.359 --> 00:00:40.840
trials the placebo pills actually outperformed
the genuine medication.

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:43.390
So how does it work?

00:00:43.390 --> 00:00:50.210
Well when we get ill or hurt ourselves, our
body puts up defences against the real problem,

00:00:50.210 --> 00:00:54.469
for example if we catch the flu our temperature
rises.

00:00:54.469 --> 00:01:00.379
But it's not the flu virus that causes this,
our body increases its internal temperature

00:01:00.379 --> 00:01:07.330
to fight off the bacteria because it knows
bacteria can't survive in a hot environment.

00:01:07.330 --> 00:01:10.940
The placebo effect breaks down these defences.

00:01:10.940 --> 00:01:17.100
Because our own body creates the symptoms,
it also has the power to get rid of them.

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:23.220
So when we're given a sugar pill and told
it will cure our illness, an authority figure,

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:29.360
in this case a doctor, has given our brain
permission to stop its defences.

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:34.910
So our symptoms get better, also, when we're
told we've been given a pill that will cure

00:01:34.910 --> 00:01:40.870
us our brain releases endorphins because it's
good news, and because endorphins are natural

00:01:40.870 --> 00:01:44.720
pain killers our symptoms improve.

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:50.700
However the placebo effect doesn't help fight
the underlying virus itself, it only helps

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:54.250
nullify the experiences of the illness.

00:01:54.250 --> 00:01:59.300
Despite this the placebo effect has been able
to produce some amazing physical results in

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:06.670
clinical trials, for example it has made warts
completely disappear and even made bald men

00:02:06.670 --> 00:02:13.090
who thought they were being given hair regrowth
serum, regrow their hair, all with the power

00:02:13.090 --> 00:02:14.390
of the mind.

00:02:14.390 --> 00:02:20.440
But the placebo effect has an evil twin, called
the nocebo effect.

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:26.030
The nocebo effect is when people are given
a harmless substance but succumb to harmful

00:02:26.030 --> 00:02:27.620
effects.

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:33.280
When patients in double-blinded clinical trials
are given sugar pills and warned of the side

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:37.340
effects they may experience if they're given
the real drug.

00:02:37.340 --> 00:02:45.710
Approximately 25% experience severe side effects,
despite the fact they're not actually taking

00:02:45.710 --> 00:02:46.910
the medication.

00:02:46.910 --> 00:02:52.760
Another, more disturbing study showed in a
group of patients about to undergo life threatening

00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:59.709
surgery, those who had convinced themselves
they were going to die usually did.

00:02:59.709 --> 00:03:05.990
Whereas patients who had a more optimistic
outlook on their surgery, usually survived.

00:03:05.990 --> 00:03:12.730
There exists a phenomena associated with the
nocebo effect called "voodoo death".

00:03:12.730 --> 00:03:18.860
This is when a person is cursed and told they
will die, and then dies.

00:03:18.860 --> 00:03:24.400
It sounds unbelievable however there have
been documented cases where patients in hospital

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:29.850
who are believed to be terminally ill and
mistakenly told they have X amount of time

00:03:29.850 --> 00:03:34.260
to live, have then died within their given
time frame.

00:03:34.260 --> 00:03:40.930
However, after death an autopsy could find
no physiological explanation for their early

00:03:40.930 --> 00:03:41.980
demise.

00:03:41.980 --> 00:03:49.349
A lot of real medication relies heavily on
the placebo effect to provide it's full benefits,

00:03:49.349 --> 00:03:52.310
this is especially true with anti-depressants.

00:03:52.310 --> 00:03:59.739
Numerous studies have shown that placebos
produce the exact same results as real anti-depressants,

00:03:59.739 --> 00:04:02.340
without any of the side effects.

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:07.940
Whilst this is good news for sufferers, these
findings have been heavily downplayed by major

00:04:07.940 --> 00:04:14.020
pharmaceutical companies who would lose out
on billions of dollars if anti-depressants

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:16.190
became less popular.

00:04:16.190 --> 00:04:22.941
Here's another fun fact, you can actually
placebo yourself into inebriation, researchers

00:04:22.941 --> 00:04:28.350
found that people who were told they had been
drinking vodka, but were really given tonic

00:04:28.350 --> 00:04:37.050
water and lime, had impaired judgement and
performed much worse on basic IQ tests.

00:04:37.050 --> 00:04:43.880
When it comes to placebo pills the properties
of the drug itself can greatly affect it's

00:04:43.880 --> 00:04:44.880
performance.

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:51.199
Researchers have found that yellow placebo
pills are the most effective at treating depression,

00:04:51.199 --> 00:04:55.780
whilst red pills cause the patient to be more
alert and awake.

00:04:55.780 --> 00:05:00.520
Green pills ease anxiety and white pills soothe
stomach pains.

00:05:00.520 --> 00:05:07.020
They also found the more placebo pills the
patient takes the more effective they are.

00:05:07.020 --> 00:05:13.990
Also pills that have a brand name printed
on them work better than those that are blank.

00:05:13.990 --> 00:05:19.070
Studies have also shown that when it comes
to over the counter medications such as paracetamol,

00:05:19.070 --> 00:05:28.360
studies have shown that a box of $3 medication
is more effective than a $0.40 box of medication,

00:05:28.360 --> 00:05:32.650
despite both products having the exact same
active ingredients.

00:05:32.650 --> 00:05:38.860
This reveals that the placebo effect is more
powerful if the perceived value of the medication

00:05:38.860 --> 00:05:40.040
is higher.

00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:46.970
But by far the biggest mystery about the placebo
effect is that it works even when you know

00:05:46.970 --> 00:05:49.240
you're taking a placebo.

00:05:49.240 --> 00:05:55.250
In clinical trials where patients are administered
a placebo then they are eventually told that

00:05:55.250 --> 00:05:58.639
they have merely been taking a sugar pill.

00:05:58.639 --> 00:06:06.320
The positive effects of the placebo remain,
with absolutely no diminishment in effectiveness.

00:06:06.320 --> 00:06:11.311
In the future this means doctors could be
prescribing sugar pills to patients, when

00:06:11.311 --> 00:06:15.020
they know full well it's a sugar pill.

00:06:15.020 --> 00:06:19.830
The placebo effect is powerful and it shows
no signs of stopping.

00:06:19.830 --> 00:06:22.950
In fact it's actually getting stronger.

00:06:22.950 --> 00:06:26.729
The placebo effect was first discovered in
the 1700s.

00:06:26.729 --> 00:06:32.860
Weirdly, it seems the more tests that medical
professionals conduct, the more powerful the

00:06:32.860 --> 00:06:36.570
placebo effect becomes over the years.

00:06:36.570 --> 00:06:40.479
It is widely thought this is because of our
growing belief in medicine.

00:06:40.479 --> 00:06:47.639
As medical technology improves, mortality
rate decreases and so our faith in the medical

00:06:47.639 --> 00:06:58.130
system increase, which subsequently increases
the power of the placebo effect.

